# Hosts outside this stack that LiteLLM may reach through Squid (e.g. an LLM
# server on the LAN), named <name>.lan.internal, in /etc/hosts format. Squid reads
# it as hosts_file; after an edit run squid/reload_squid.sh. Besides .env, this is
# the only place where IP addresses are written. Example:
#   <ip-address>  llm.lan.internal
